      "side": 1,
      "message": "A couple reasons. First, this topic is attempting to consume a kernel platform build directly without need for manual intermediary steps. The uapi headers rule in kleaf outputs a tar.gz, not an include folder. The pixel prebuilt kernel repos have a kernel-headers folder that previously had clean_header.py ran on them. Thus a rule is needed to extract the headers plus run the clean. The vendor/lineage change that adds this rule does so.\n\nhttps://github.com/search?q\u003dorg%3ALineageOS%20generated_kernel_headers\u0026type\u003dcode\nSecondly, there\u0027s a bunch of stuff using genenerated_kernel_headers directly. This change replaces those as well. It could be argued that all of these should be converted to device_kernel_headers if a device changes to kernel-platform, and that\u0027s valid. But this is attempting to allow replacement with as little modifications as possible.",
